<article class="env-lemma" id="0BGR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BGR">Lemma <span data-tag="0BGR">65.11.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. Let $G$ be an algebraic space over $S$, let $F$ be a sheaf on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$, and let $G \to F$ be a representable transformation of functors which is surjective and étale. Then $F$ is an algebraic space. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Pick a scheme $U$ and a surjective étale morphism $U \to G$. Since $G$ is an algebraic space $U \to G$ is representable. Hence the composition $U \to G \to F$ is representable, surjective, and étale. See Lemmas <a href="/tag/02WA" data-tag="02WA">65.3.2</a> and <a href="/tag/02WK" data-tag="02WK">65.5.4</a>. Thus $F$ is an algebraic space by Lemma <a href="/tag/0BGQ" data-tag="0BGQ">65.11.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>